{"id": "4d4ee691-5942-4f5b-878a-17674c65d836", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T04:19:24Z", "level": "info", "message": "The spec file has been created at `docs/ai/stories/DS-02/spec.md` (61 lines, well within the 150-line limit).\n\nHere's what the spec covers:\n\n**New components to create:**\n- `src/Sidebar.js` — collapsible sidebar with Dashboard/Orders navigation links\n- `src/Orders.js` — mock orders table with client-side search\n\n**Existing files to update:**\n- `src/App.js` — add `/orders` route to `renderView`\n- `src/Dashboard.js` — integrate the sidebar alongside existing content\n- `src/App.css` — add all new styles (sidebar, orders table, search input)\n- `docs/ai/context-map.json` — add `/orders` to `knownPaths`\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- Sidebar rendered inside both Dashboard and Orders (not a global wrapper)\n- Sidebar defaults to expanded, collapse state is local `useState` (not persisted)\n- Existing top-right nav bar (profile, settings, logout) stays unchanged\n- All styles in `App.css` only — governance-compliant\n- No new dependencies, no react-router, no TypeScript\n\n**One blocking open question flagged:** whether the sidebar should also appear on `/settings` and `/profile`. This needs clarification before implementation proceeds.", "stepKey": "story_analyzer"}
