{"id": "94e3fa3b-a041-44e2-beb8-ebcf582dbb28", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T04:20:25Z", "level": "info", "message": "The implementation plan has been written to `docs/ai/stories/DS-02/implementation-plan.md`. Here's a summary of what it covers:\n\n**8 target files** (4 create, 4 modify):\n\n| Action | File | Why |\n|--------|------|-----|\n| Create | `src/Sidebar.js` | Collapsible nav sidebar component |\n| Create | `src/Orders.js` | Orders page with searchable mock table |\n| Create | `src/Sidebar.test.js` | Smoke + collapse toggle tests |\n| Create | `src/Orders.test.js` | Smoke + table render + search filter tests |\n| Modify | `src/App.js` | Register `/orders` route |\n| Modify | `src/Dashboard.js` | Integrate sidebar alongside existing content |\n| Modify | `src/App.css` | Sidebar, orders table, and search styles |\n| Modify | `docs/ai/context-map.json` | Add `\"/orders\"` to knownPaths |\n\n**9 ordered steps** — from creating components through route registration, styling, tests, and final validation (`npm test -- --watchAll=false` + `npx react-scripts build`).\n\nKey decisions encoded from the spec:\n- Sidebar uses local `useState` (no localStorage persistence), default expanded\n- Sidebar rendered inside both Dashboard and Orders (no global layout wrapper)\n- Dashboard's top-right nav bar remains unchanged\n- All styles go into `App.css` (no new CSS files, per governance)\n- Mock orders data is an inline array in `Orders.js`", "stepKey": "implementation_planner"}
