{"id": "218287c6-3cdb-4a90-a5b5-67f41afd38be", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T04:26:12Z", "level": "info", "message": "All 9 tests pass and build compiles successfully. Let me compile the review.\n\nNow comparing the full implementation against the spec, plan, and governance rules:\n\n**Acceptance criteria verification:**\n- ✅ Sidebar renders on `/dashboard` and collapses/expands via toggle button\n- ✅ Sidebar \"Dashboard\" link navigates to `/dashboard`; \"Orders\" link navigates to `/orders`\n- ✅ `/orders` route renders a table with 5 mock order rows (ID, Customer, Product, Status, Date)\n- ✅ Search input filters rows in real time as user types\n- ✅ Sidebar and orders page gated by existing auth guard\n\n**Governance check:**\n- ✅ No react-router (pushState preserved)\n- ✅ No TypeScript\n- ✅ No new CSS files (all styles in App.css)\n- ✅ No backend/API code\n- ✅ No Dockerfile changes\n- ✅ Functional components + hooks pattern preserved\n\n---\n\n## Findings\n\n- id: R1\n  severity: LOW\n  file: package.json\n  evidence: 3 new devDependencies (`@testing-library/jest-dom`, `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event`) were added. `src/setupTests.js` was also created. Neither was listed in the plan's target files, and step 9 of the plan explicitly says \"Confirm no new dependencies.\" These packages are necessary for the `toBeInTheDocument()` matchers and `render()` calls used in `Orders.test.js` and `Sidebar.test.js`, but their addition was undocumented and unjustified in the implementation.\n  fix: Update the plan to acknowledge these as expected CRA-standard test dependencies, or add a justification comment in the commit message. These are the same packages CRA 5 ships by default — they restore standard CRA test infrastructure.\n\nNo regressions detected — there are no pre-existing tests to break. All 9 new tests pass. Build compiles with no errors. No BLOCKER or HIGH severity issues found.\n\nNow I'll write the final summary.", "stepKey": "final_review"}
{"id": "4449dcb6-5a9c-438c-bacc-63227d4ae293", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T04:26:16Z", "level": "info", "message": "## Review Complete\n\n**Findings: 1 issue (LOW severity)**\n\n- **R1** — 3 devDependencies (`@testing-library/jest-dom`, `@testing-library/react`, `@testing-library/user-event`) and `src/setupTests.js` were added outside the plan's target files and without justification. These are standard CRA test infrastructure packages needed for the tests to function, but their addition constitutes plan drift. Fix: acknowledge them in the plan or add a justification note.\n\n**All acceptance criteria met. 9/9 tests pass. Build succeeds.** No regressions, no governance violations, no BLOCKER/HIGH issues.\n\nFinal summary written to `.opencode/executions/exec-e05d8ac6-06ea-41e8-8eb6-282b5b4129a0/final-summary.md`.", "stepKey": "final_review"}
